^["intent"]{
 ~#goal: "A >>[stamp] type — prose line is a construct of the language, not of plan files: it reads as one entry in every dialect, so neither a caller's path nor a pragma decides whether stream prose is an error."
 ~#was: "Parse health on plan files should report structure, not stream prose; the lexer owned a >>[ line only under Spw.p, and the health probe parses without the path."
 ~#taste: "measure the thing, not the lens: a health verdict must not depend on whether the caller remembered to pass a path"
}

