 ~[stream_line_census]: "![seed] — fixture over every line-start >>[ outside .agents: 13 files with their dialect, tokens and errors today (sense-loop.spw 6, portrait.prompt.spw 3); the negative control for ~[entry_line_all_dialects]"
 ~[stream_line_theory]: ".[theory] — docs/theory/spw/stream-lines.spw: an entry appended to its frame; a dated stamp is a log line, an ordinal a beat; the body is prose; how >>[ sits beside << >> streams"
 ~[register_stream_entry]: "#[experimental] — =exp[id: stream.entry_line] registered as proposed in SYNTAX_CATALOG, citing the theory note"
 ~[entry_line_all_dialects]: "^seed[lexer] — readPlanStreamEntry runs in every dialect, not only under planStream; the census errors go to 0, every other token is byte-identical, plan-stream.test.ts is unchanged"
 ~[stamp_kinds]: "vocab[seed] — conditional on ?[stamp_kinds]: an entry states its stamp kind (time, day, ordinal, other) so the LSP and writers stop re-deriving it"
 ~[entry_body_refs]: "^seed[lexer] — conditional on ?[body_reading]: refs inside an entry body lex as their own tokens within the prose"
 ~[editor_grammar_parity]: "![editors] — VS Code, IntelliJ and Neovim highlight a line-start entry in every .spw as the lexer reads it; the VS Code grammar fixture already does outside plans"
